# Credit Recommendation Engine — environment configuration (example)
#
# The app reads plain environment variables (no .env auto-loading yet).
# PowerShell:   $env:CREDIT_ENGINE_DATABASE_URL = "..."
# bash:         export CREDIT_ENGINE_DATABASE_URL="..."
#
# Unset → the app runs fully in-memory (demo personas, in-memory outbox).
# Set  → main.py wires SqlPersonRepository + SqlOutbox at startup.

# Azure SQL Server via pymssql (no system ODBC driver needed; pip install .[mssql]).
# URL-encode special characters in the password (@ → %40, { → %7B, etc.):
#CREDIT_ENGINE_DATABASE_URL=mssql+pymssql://USER:URLENCODED_PASSWORD@YOURSERVER.database.windows.net:1433/CreditEngine

# Azure SQL Server via pyodbc (requires "ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server" installed):
#CREDIT_ENGINE_DATABASE_URL=mssql+pyodbc://USER:URLENCODED_PASSWORD@YOURSERVER.database.windows.net:1433/CreditEngine?driver=ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server&Encrypt=yes

# Local SQLite (the default when the variable is unset):
#CREDIT_ENGINE_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///credit_engine.db

# Azure SQL checklist:
#  1. Azure Portal → SQL server → Networking → add your client IP to the firewall
#  2. python scripts/apply_schema.py --url "..."      (tables, CHECKs, indexes)
#  3. python scripts/generate_data.py --url "..." --replace   (load the 20K personas)
#  4. Set CREDIT_ENGINE_DATABASE_URL and start the API
